/* dig.js — Dr. Quartz's Dig Site: the science area (Oct 2026). Replaces the old Lab front, the Science Cave trips, the Crystal Garden
   (switched off, kept in saves) and Ozzy's Inner Space (switched off). Reached by train (train.js → go('lab')).
   Side view of a 50-row rock column in time order (Soil → Ice Age → Late Cretaceous → Late Jurassic → Triassic → Ancient sea → Bedrock),
   tap-to-dig with gravity, ladders, one Energy bar, Dr. Quartz's rope rescue, fossils taken out the scientist's way (map, uncover, glue,
   plaster jacket; K–2 4 steps, 3–5 and 6+ 7) or rushed, small finds by layer, a field notebook ("Which is older?", "What was this place like?"),
   identifying each bone from clues ("What is it?") and a museum of 8-bone skeletons plus a sticker book.
   Workshopped with simulated experts (paleontologists, a preparator, museum educator, teachers: 9/10) and kids (9.3/10).
   Save: p.dig = {site:{seed,dug,lad,xf,ex} (bitsets), mus:{d:{id:{have[8],perfect,done}},f:{name:count},careful}, wb:[bones to identify], pick, met}.
   Uses Math Quest globals: MQP(), save(), toast(), go(), app, SCREENS, modal, closeModal, esc, fxVol, SFX, W, HeroPuppet, CharPuppet, MQ_PONDPETS, CAVE_DATA, Lab, Quartz, Inner. */
/* Dig 2.0 mockup — Dr. Quartz's new dig site (workshopped design, final v3).
   Side view with real gravity; tap a highlighted tile next to you to dig it or step into it; tap along your row to walk there;
   ladders go in automatically when you climb (you carry a few); one Energy bar (digging uses it; the lift always comes);
   depth layers get dimmer but never black, and glow with crystals and glowworms; cracked rock only breaks if you step back on it;
   fossils: brush them out carefully or smash them free with the pickaxe (a smashed one loses a clue). */
